<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Pontotoc Creek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Pontotoc <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, signed on 20 October 1832 at Pontotoc, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, ceded the remaining Chickasaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> east of the Mississippi to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The land was to be surveyed and sold, with the proceeds held for the nation, while the Chickasaw sought a new home in the west. They moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a> from 1837, settling at first among the Choctaw.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pontotoc-creek.jpg" alt="Treaty of Pontotoc Creek" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Woolley · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chickasaw_Tribe_Mississippi_1832.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
